{
 "construction": "Chunked content-key blob encryption and dag-pb root block",
 "spec": "\u00a714.3.4 Blobs; \u00a713.3 label 'agora/chunk/v1'; \u00a713.1 Content identifiers",
 "notes": [
  "Fixed inputs named by a label are SHA-256(UTF-8(\"agora-test-vectors/\" || label)), truncated to the stated length.",
  "contentKey is fixed here; the spec requires a fresh random key per file.",
  "Chunk size is fixed at 262,144 bytes by the spec (Appendix C), so the multi-chunk cases use 263,144-byte (2 chunks) and 524,293-byte (3 chunks) files.",
  "nonce[i] = i as 96-bit big-endian; aad[i] = \"agora/chunk/v1\" || uint64be(i) || uint64be(n) || uint8(final). block = ciphertext || 16-byte tag.",
  "Blocks longer than 4096 bytes are given as blockLength, blockSha256Hex and their first and last 64 bytes; the check scripts recompute each full block and compare its SHA-256.",
  "Root block (n > 1): dag-pb PBNode with Links before Data; each PBLink = Hash (binary chunk CID), Name (present, zero length), Tsize (block length). Data = UnixFS Type=File(2), filesize = sum of block lengths, one non-packed blocksizes entry per block. Root CID = CIDv1 dag-pb (0x70) sha2-256. blobIdText is the root CID for n > 1, else the chunk CID."
 ],
